  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.2.0: Generic chunks. ProcessAsync now produces RetrievalChunk<TRecord> chunks whose Record is the strongly typed source record — read chunk.Record.Id instead of chunk.Record[\"Id\"]. The result set stays non-generic (RetrievalResults): IList<T> is invariant, so a typed Chunks view could only be a stale copy; cast the chunks with chunks.Cast<RetrievalChunk<TRecord>>(). A keySelector parameter (Func<TRecord, object?>) states how fusion deduplicates; return the key value itself — no ToString() needed, since keys are compared by their own equality. By default it reads the record's Key/Id, falling back to the chunk text. Only the collection overload fills the supplementary dictionary (record members + parent/child aliases) that the record-agnostic result processors read — on the custom-search overload the caller owns the chunks and maps its own record. ChunkIdentity was removed. The non-generic ProcessAsync overloads and the base RetrievalChunk type are unchanged, so existing callers and the record-agnostic result processors keep working.",
